# Frontend Development Patterns

## React Components
- Use functional components with TypeScript
- Hooks: useState, useEffect, useQuery (React Query)
- Props interfaces defined above component
- Example:
```typescript
interface ComponentNameProps {
  id: number
  onAction: (value: string) => void
}

export default function ComponentName({ id, onAction }: ComponentNameProps) {
  // Component logic
}
```

## State Management
- React Query for server state
- Local state with useState for UI state
- Query keys pattern: `['resource', id, params]`

## API Integration
- All API calls through [frontend/src/services/api.ts](mdc:frontend/src/services/api.ts)
- Use axios interceptors for error handling
- Handle loading, error, and success states

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS for all styling
- Dark mode by default with theme toggle
- Utility-first approach, minimal custom CSS

## Error Handling
- Display errors with [frontend/src/components/ErrorDisplay.tsx](mdc:frontend/src/components/ErrorDisplay.tsx)
- Toast notifications for success/error feedback
- Graceful fallbacks for failed API calls

## TypeScript
- Strict mode enabled
- Define interfaces for all API responses
- Avoid `any` type - use proper types or `unknown`